<title>USA: Allied Waste Q4 oper revenue rises.</title>
<headline>Allied Waste Q4 oper revenue rises.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				  Three Months	Twelve Months</p>
<p>			     Ended December 31,  Ended December 31,</p>
<p>				  1996     1995	   1996     1995</p>
<p>As Reported:</p>
<p> Operating Revenues     $62,783 $55,634     $246,679 $217,544</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)     (78,199)   2,101     (79,427)   12,381</p>
<p> Earnings(Loss) Share    (1.29)  (0.03)	 (1.38)     0.15</p>
<p> Avg shares		  60,564  40,067	 58,423   40,046</p>
<p>Excluding Non-Recurring Items:</p>
<p> Net Income		   2,681   2,383	 17,218   13,164</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share	  0.04    0.03	   0.27     0.23</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name of company is Allied Waste Industries Inc.</p>
<p>In connection with its purchase of the solid waste division of Laidlaw Inc in Q4 the company incurred about $84.7 million in acquisition-related charges and a $3.9 million pre-tax extraordinary loss for refinancing.</p>
<p>It also recorded a $5.7 million provision during Q4 for other non-recurring items.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
